<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miura et al. (2009) & Jaslow (1990) cranial suture fractal interdigitation and Kuramoto-Sivashinsky osteogenic instability — MorphoEval overall 56.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline assessment of `2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py` (57.3/100). The baseline script implements a 1D single-valued linear spectral amplification of the Kuramoto-Sivashinsky dispersion relation omega(k) = alpha*k^2 - beta*k^4 - gamma for sagittal vs mechanically unloaded sutures, but omits the nonlinear KPZ normal-growth coupling (v_0/2)*(dh/dx)^2, 2D bidirectional overhanging phase-field / normal-front interdigitation (needed to reach SII > 2.5 and box-counting fractal dimension D_f ~ 1.35), infant neonatal, adult lambdoid, and FGFR2 Apert craniosynostosis regimes, Jaslow (1990) bending energy absorption quantification, and automated CV suture trace segmentation on `human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg`. Overall 56.3/100 (faithfulness 53.9, reproducibility 62.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 50, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 54, Source and data traceability 66, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: docs/media/allometric_cranial_sutures_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 422533 B, 1380×936 px, artifact_sha256 bffa061ad0a44e38fe57ca06bf134f023c0e26e4242d60e84e75b515230ce928 (sha256 bffa061ad0a44e38fe57ca06bf134f023c0e26e4242d60e84e75b515230ce928), spec_fingerprint 53dc68ef4189bb186f820ba54b5a160dfe42da44326e82b66ab860cc7d2ad00e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 53dc68ef4189bb186f820ba54b5a160dfe42da44326e82b66ab860cc7d2ad00e; artifact_sha256: bffa061ad0a44e38fe57ca06bf134f023c0e26e4242d60e84e75b515230ce928; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/allometric_cranial_sutures_reference.json=dbb634957fb6941d..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg=b3c411a6a4713770..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/paper_citations.bib=bffc86bbbd2dd3d6..., datasets/allometric_cranial_sutures/scout_manifest.json=226c072307597439...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add automated CV extraction of the sagittal suture trace on `human_sagittal_suture_specimen.jpg`, measure empirical box-counting fractal dimension D_f and SII, and render a 9-panel dark-mode comparison figure and 24-frame animated GIF.",
        "remediation needed: Implement pseudo-spectral semi-implicit / ETDRK4 Kuramoto-Sivashinsky + KPZ nonlinear normal-growth cascade and 2D bidirectional overhanging phase-field / normal-front interdigitation producing multi-valued suture fingers with D_f ~ 1.35 and SII > 2.5.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate all 5 canonical regimes (infant neonatal flat suture, adult sagittal fractal suture, adult lambdoid hyper-interdigitated suture, mechanical unloading null control, and FGFR2 Apert craniosynostosis fusion) plus a 15x15 (alpha, beta) morphospace and Jaslow (1990) bending energy curve." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.63e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

